meta {
  name: Login (rate limited)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "username": "{{username}}",
    "password": "{{badPassword}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 429
  res.body.type: contains rate-limited
  res.body.title: isString
  res.body.status: eq 429
}

docs {
  Login while the (IP, username) bucket is exhausted — expect 429
  rate-limited.

  The bucket is 5 attempts / minute / (IP, username), shared across
  bad-password and good-password attempts. To reproduce from clean:
  fire 5 login-bad-password.bru requests in the same minute from
  the same machine, then run this.

  Or, for the same effect without burning 5 Bruno runs, hit the
  endpoint 5+ times with curl:
      for i in 1 2 3 4 5 6; do
        curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' \
          -X POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login \
          -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
          -d '{"username":"alice","password":"wrong"}'
      done

  Bucket refills smoothly, so this test is only valid within a
  minute of exhausting it.
}